From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: report firmware crashes before QMI ready

An MHI RDDM notification received during initial firmware boot only emits a
debug message. Recovery is then skipped because QMI firmware ready has not
completed, leaving the later WMI ready timeout as the first visible error.

Report the RDDM transition and explain why early recovery is skipped so the
actual firmware failure is visible without enabling the full debug mask.
Collect the crash dump before returning because the normal recovery path,
which performs the collection, cannot run until QMI firmware ready completes.

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c | 4 +++-
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c  | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/core.c
@@ -1684,7 +1684,9 @@ static void ath12k_core_reset(struct wor
 	long time_left;
 
 	if (!(test_bit(ATH12K_FLAG_QMI_FW_READY_COMPLETE, &ab->dev_flags))) {
-		ath12k_warn(ab, "ignore reset dev flags 0x%lx\n", ab->dev_flags);
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "firmware crashed before QMI ready; recovery skipped (dev flags 0x%lx)\n",
+			    ab->dev_flags);
+		ath12k_coredump_collect(ab);
 		return;
 	}
 
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath12k/mhi.c
@@ -149,6 +149,8 @@ static void ath12k_mhi_op_status_cb(stru
 		ath12k_warn(ab, "firmware crashed: MHI_CB_SYS_ERROR\n");
 		break;
 	case MHI_CB_EE_RDDM:
+		ath12k_warn(ab, "firmware crashed: MHI_CB_EE_RDDM\n");
+
 		if (ab_pci->mhi_pre_cb == MHI_CB_EE_RDDM) {
 			ath12k_dbg(ab, ATH12K_DBG_BOOT,
 				   "do not queue again for consecutive RDDM event\n");
